'''Andrew Bazzi''' ({{ipac-en|ˈ|b|ɑː|z|i}}; {{respell|BAH|zee}} born August 28, 1997), known [[mononym]]ously by his surname '''Bazzi''',<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sxLwWX2znFA|title=15 Things About 'Honest' Singer Bazzi You Should Know!|publisher=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|via=[[YouTube]]|date=April 16, 2018|access-date=May 6, 2020}} ''His name is pronounced at the start of the video.''</ref><ref name="BillMeet">{{cite magazine| last =Weatherby| first =Taylor| title =Meet Bazzi, the 20-Year-Old Rising Pop Star Who's Taking the Hot 100 by Storm With 'Mine'| magazine =Billboard| date =February 16, 2018| url =https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/bazzi-interview-mine-hot-100-streaming-8100013/| access-date =March 6, 2018| archive-date =March 31, 2019| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20190331165752/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop/8100013/bazzi-interview-mine-hot-100-streaming| url-status =live}}</ref> is an American singer-songwriter.<ref name="billboard debut">{{Cite magazine |last=Zellner |first=Xander |date=January 31, 2018 |title=Bazzi Makes Billboard Hot 100 Debut With 'Mine' |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/bazzi-mine-hot-100-debut-streaming-numbers/ |magazine=Billboard |access-date=April 25, 2018 |archive-date=April 23, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180423033143/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/chart-beat/8097385/bazzi-mine-hot-100-debut-streaming-numbers |url-status=live }}</ref> His song "[[Mine (Bazzi song)|Mine]]", released in October 2017, gained popularity in early 2018 when it became a [[meme]] through [[Musical.ly]] edits, and the use of a [[Snapchat]] lens filter featuring the song. It peaked at number 11 on the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]], and appeared on several international charts. He released his debut studio album ''[[Cosmic (album)|Cosmic]]'' in 2018, which peaked at number 14 on the [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]] chart.

==Early life and education==
Bazzi was born in [[Canton, Michigan]].<ref name="iheart"/> His mother is American and his father is a [[Lebanese people|Lebanese]] immigrant. He has lived in [[Beirut]] and has Lebanese nationality. He grew up in [[Dearborn, Michigan]].<ref>{{cite web|title=BAZZI|url=http://artistpg.com/partner/bazzi/|website=Artist Partner Group|access-date=August 17, 2020|archive-date=November 27, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201127135750/http://artistpg.com/partner/bazzi/|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Ryan |first=Patrick |title=Everything you need to know about Bazzi, the voice behind viral sensation 'Mine' |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/music/2018/04/15/everything-you-need-know-bazzi-voice-behind-viral-sensation-mine/508097002/ |access-date=2024-01-19 |website=USA TODAY |language=en-US}}</ref> He learned to speak [[Arabic]] and played the [[kazoo]], [[oud]], and [[guitar]] as a child.<ref name="Apple">{{cite news| last =Yeung| first =Neil Z.| title =Bazzi on Apple Music| publisher =Apple Music| url =https://music.apple.com/us/artist/bazzi/800263205| access-date =March 6, 2018| archive-date =May 2, 2019| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20190502224432/https://itunes.apple.com/us/artist/bazzi/800263205| url-status =live}}</ref><ref name="BWW">{{cite news| title =Bazzi Takes Over The Charts With MINE| work =Broadway World| date =February 14, 2018| url =https://www.broadwayworld.com/bwwmusic/article/Bazzi-Takes-Over-The-Charts-With-MINE-20180214| access-date =March 6, 2018| archive-date =June 12, 2018| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20180612142531/https://www.broadwayworld.com/bwwmusic/article/Bazzi-Takes-Over-The-Charts-With-MINE-20180214| url-status =live}}</ref> In 2012, he began posting covers of songs on his [[YouTube]] channel. He attended [[Plymouth-Canton Educational Park]]. In November 2014, he moved to the [[Los Angeles]] area to pursue a music career. He finished high school at [[Santa Monica High School]] in 2015.<ref name="Samohi">{{cite news| last =Young| first =Nico| title =Andrew Bazzi| newspaper =The Samohi| date =March 27, 2015| url =http://www.thesamohi.com/ae/andrew-bazzi| access-date =March 6, 2018| archive-date =February 14, 2018| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20180214073745/http://www.thesamohi.com/ae/andrew-bazzi| url-status =live}}</ref>

==Career==
Bazzi created a [[Vine (service)|Vine]] account in July 2013.<ref name="Samohi"/> By 2015, he had accrued 1.5 million followers on the site. In September of that year, he became the first artist to release a Vine "Featured Track" which was entitled, "Bring You Home".<ref name="Bill15">{{cite magazine| last =McCall| first =Malorie| title =Andrew Bazzi Is First Artist to Debut a Song as a Vine 'Featured Track': Watch| magazine =Billboard| date =September 25, 2015| url =https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/andrew-bazzi-vine-featured-track-6708084/| access-date =March 6, 2018| archive-date =May 20, 2018| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20180520104708/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop-shop/6708084/andrew-bazzi-vine-featured-track| url-status =live}}</ref> In 2016, he was featured on the Fancy Cars' track "Fun".<ref name="Apple"/> Over the course of the next two years, Bazzi released several singles including "Alone" "[[Beautiful (Bazzi song)|Beautiful]]",<ref name="VMag">{{cite news| last =Viswanath| first =Jake| title =Bazzi Wants to Make You "Mine" With His New Single| publisher =V| date =October 12, 2017| url =https://vmagazine.com/article/bazzi-wants-make-mine-new-single/| access-date =March 6, 2018| archive-date =February 12, 2018| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20180212201701/https://vmagazine.com/article/bazzi-wants-make-mine-new-single/| url-status =live}}</ref> "Got Friends", and "Sober".<ref name="Gambiarra">{{cite news| last =Firayama| first =Wester| title =Conheça Bazzi, dono do viral 'Mine', o hit que ganhou o mundo| language =pt| publisher =A Gambiarra| date =February 6, 2018| url =https://www.agambiarra.com/conheca-bazzi-hit-viral-mine/| access-date =March 6, 2018| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20180613234411/https://www.agambiarra.com/conheca-bazzi-hit-viral-mine/| archive-date =June 13, 2018| url-status =dead}}</ref> Bazzi has cited artists [[Justin Timberlake]], [[Bryson Tiller]], [[Duran Duran]], [[Michael Jackson]] and [[Guns N' Roses]] among his influences.<ref name="iheart">{{Cite news |url=https://channel955.iheart.com/featured/joey-radio/content/2018-04-30-bazzi-announces-his-cosmic-tour/ |title=Bazzi Announces His Cosmic Tour |date=April 30, 2018 |work=[[WKQI]] |access-date=July 3, 2018 |archive-date=July 4, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180704010106/https://channel955.iheart.com/featured/joey-radio/content/2018-04-30-bazzi-announces-his-cosmic-tour/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.allmusic.com/artist/bazzi-mn0003673291/biography |title=Artist Biography |last=Yeung |first=Neil Z. |work=[[AllMusic]] |access-date=2018-07-03 |archive-date=2018-07-04 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180704034638/https://www.allmusic.com/artist/bazzi-mn0003673291/biography |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.capitalfm.com/news/music/who-is-bazzi/|title=Who Is Bazzi? Everything You Need To Know About The 'Beautiful' Star|website=Capital|access-date=April 27, 2020|archive-date=October 9, 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191009054507/https://www.capitalfm.com/news/music/who-is-bazzi/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In October 2017, he released the single "[[Mine (Bazzi song)|Mine]]".<ref name="VMag"/> Within days of its release, an A&R executive at [[Warner Music Group|Warner Music]]-affiliated [[Artist Partner Group]] had signed him to a deal including his songwriter Henry Fredrickson from Minnesota.<ref>{{cite news| last =Aswad| first =Jem| title =Bazzi on 'Mine,' Becoming a Solo Star and What He Learned From Justin Timberlake| work =[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]| date =November 29, 2018| url =https://variety.com/2018/music/features/bazzi-mine-solo-career-justin-timberlake-1203038597/| access-date =April 20, 2019| archive-date =April 27, 2019| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20190427103013/https://variety.com/2018/music/features/bazzi-mine-solo-career-justin-timberlake-1203038597/| url-status =live}}</ref> The song increased in popularity after becoming an Internet meme,<ref name="Genius">{{cite news| last =Mench| first =Chris| title =How Pop Singer-Songwriter Bazzi Rode Viral Success To A Budding Hit Single With "Mine"| publisher =Genius| date =February 6, 2018| url =https://genius.com/a/how-pop-singer-songwriter-bazzi-rode-viral-success-to-a-budding-hit-single-with-mine| access-date =March 6, 2018| archive-date =February 14, 2018| archive-url =https://web.archive.org/web/20180214073420/https://genius.com/a/how-pop-singer-songwriter-bazzi-rode-viral-success-to-a-budding-hit-single-with-mine| url-status =live}}</ref> through videos featuring a slideshow of different pictures of the subject of the video with the [[Snapchat]] "hearts" filter and overlaying lyrics.<ref name="Dot">{{cite news| last=Hathaway| first=Jay| title='Precious when you smile' is the first big Snapchat meme of the year| work=The Daily Dot| date=February 1, 2018| url=https://www.dailydot.com/unclick/precious-when-you-smile-meme/| access-date=March 6, 2018| archive-date=February 13, 2018| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180213021550/https://www.dailydot.com/unclick/precious-when-you-smile-meme/| url-status=live}}</ref> In January 2018, the song appeared on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]], debuting at number 56.<ref name="BillDebut">{{cite magazine| last=Zellner| first=Xander| title=Bazzi Makes Billboard Hot 100 Debut With 'Mine'| magazine=Billboard| date=January 31, 2018| url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/bazzi-mine-hot-100-debut-streaming-numbers/| access-date=March 6, 2018| archive-date=February 9, 2018| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180209001250/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/chart-beat/8097385/bazzi-mine-hot-100-debut-streaming-numbers| url-status=live}}</ref> As of April 2018, the song's peak on the list was number 11.<ref name="Hot100peak">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/drake-gods-plan-hot-100-number-one-tenth-week/|title=Drake Becomes First Lead Solo Male With Two 10-Week Billboard Hot 100 No. 1s, as 'God's Plan' Stays at the Summit|magazine=Billboard|last=Trust|first=Gary|date=April 2, 2018|access-date=April 3, 2018|archive-date=April 2, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180402211408/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/chart-beat/8280590/drake-gods-plan-hot-100-number-one-tenth-week|url-status=live}}</ref> Bazzi also released three new singles in 2018, "Why?",<ref name="BWW"/> "Gone" and "Honest".<ref name="BillGone">{{cite magazine| last=Hussein| first=Wandera| title=Bazzi Flows About Moving Forward on the Hip-Hop Tinged 'Gone'| magazine=Billboard| date=February 21, 2018| url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/bazzi-new-song-gone-8213447/| access-date=March 6, 2018| archive-date=May 14, 2018| archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180514030913/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop/8213447/bazzi-new-song-gone| url-status=live}}</ref> On March 13, 2018, Bazzi was announced as the special guest on [[Camila Cabello]]'s Never Be the Same Tour's North American leg.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Camila_Cabello/status/973701998435422208|title=I'm so excited to announce that one of my favorite new artists @bazzi ✨will be my special guest on the North American leg of my Never Be The Same Tour 🔮🔮🔮|last=@Camila_Cabello|date=2018-03-13|website=[[Twitter]]|access-date=2018-03-15}}</ref> On April 17, 2018, ''[[Cosmic (album)|Cosmic]]'' debuted at number 35 and later peaked at number 14 on the US [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]] albums chart.<ref name="BB200">{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/charts/billboard-200/2018-04-28|title=Billboard 200: April 24, 2018|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|access-date=April 25, 2018|archive-date=May 20, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180520044000/https://www.billboard.com/charts/billboard-200/2018-04-28|url-status=live}}</ref> Bazzi joined Justin Timberlake's [[Man of the Woods Tour]] as the opening act for the European leg.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.billboard.com/media/podcasts/pop-shop-podcast-bazzi-interview-cosmic-album-camila-cabello-tour-justin-timberlake-8468052/ |title=Pop Shop Podcast: Bazzi on His 'Cosmic' Journey, Connecting With Camila Cabello & Chance Encounter With Justin Timberlake |last1=Caulfield |first1=Keith |last2=Atkinson |first2=Katie |date=July 31, 2018 |magazine=Billboard |access-date=July 31, 2018 |archive-date=August 1, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180801095828/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/podcasts/8468052/pop-shop-podcast-bazzi-interview-cosmic-album-camila-cabello-tour-justin-timberlake |url-status=live }}</ref> He received a nomination for an [[MTV Video Music Award for Best New Artist]].<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/cardi-b-the-carters-childish-gambino-drake-lead-2018-vma-nominations-699523/|title=VMAs 2018: Cardi B, the Carters, Childish Gambino, Drake Lead Nominations|date=July 16, 2018|access-date=July 17, 2018|first=Ryan|last=Reed|magazine=Rolling Stone|archive-date=July 17, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180717145353/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/cardi-b-the-carters-childish-gambino-drake-lead-2018-vma-nominations-699523/|url-status=live}}</ref> Bazzi collaborated with [[Camila Cabello]] on a remix of the song "[[Beautiful (Bazzi song)|Beautiful]]", which was released on August 2, 2018.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/bazzi-camila-cabello-beautiful-remix-with-8468322/|title=Bazzi Teams Up With Camila Cabello For Angelic 'Beautiful' Remix: Listen|date=August 2, 2018|access-date=August 2, 2018|first=Whittum|last=Connor|magazine=Billboard|archive-date=August 2, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180802205132/https://www.billboard.com/articles/columns/pop/8468322/bazzi-camila-cabello-beautiful-remix-with|url-status=live}}</ref> Bazzi performed "Beautiful" on a float in the 2018 [[Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade]].<ref>{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/photos/8486310/2018-macys-thanksgiving-parade-photos-of-diana-ross-kelly-clarkson-more|title=2018 Macy's Thanksgiving Parade: Photos of Diana Ross, Kelly Clarkson & More!|magazine=Billboard|access-date=2019-04-07|archive-date=2019-04-05|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190405152919/https://www.billboard.com/photos/8486310/2018-macys-thanksgiving-parade-photos-of-diana-ross-kelly-clarkson-more|url-status=live}}</ref>

Bazzi worked with K-pop entertainment company [[SM Entertainment]] to co-write songs for two of their boy bands, [[Exo|EXO]] and [[NCT Dream]]. With NCT Dream, he co-wrote "We Go Up" with their member Mark for the EP, ''[[We Go Up (NCT Dream EP)|We Go Up]]''. With EXO, he co-wrote "The Eve" for the studio album ''[[The War (album)|The War]]'', and "Ooh La La La" and "Oasis" for the studio album ''[[Don't Mess Up My Tempo|Don’t Mess Up My Tempo]]''.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Bell |first1=Crystal |title=Bazzi Wrote NCT Dream's New Single 'We Go Up' And It's A Total Earworm |url=http://www.mtv.com/news/3098557/nct-dream-bazzi-we-go-up/ |website=MTV |access-date=1 September 2018 |archive-date=1 September 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180901044605/http://www.mtv.com/news/3098557/nct-dream-bazzi-we-go-up/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=DON'T MESS UP MY TEMPO – The 5th Album by EXO|website=[[iTunes]] |date=2018-11-02|url=https://music.apple.com/au/album/dont-mess-up-my-tempo-the-5th-album/1440782229|language=en-AU|access-date=2018-11-03|archive-date=2018-11-03|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181103210430/https://itunes.apple.com/au/album/dont-mess-up-my-tempo-the-5th-album/1440782229|url-status=live}}</ref> He additionally co-wrote the song "[[Love Shot (Exo song)|Love Shot]]" for the repackaged version of ''Don't Mess Up My Tempo'', ''[[Love Shot (Exo album)|Love Shot]]''.<ref>{{cite web|title=LOVE SHOT – The 5th Album Repackage – EP by EXO|website=[[Apple Music]] |date=2024-07-08|url=https://music.apple.com/au/album/love-shot/1446231540?i=1446231541|language=en-AU|access-date=2024-07-08|archive-date=2022-03-27|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220327031144/https://music.apple.com/au/album/love-shot/1446231540?i=1446231541|url-status=live}}</ref> He also co-wrote song "[[Give Me a Chance (Lay song)|Give Me a Chance]]" with Chinese singer and Exo member [[Lay (entertainer)|Lay Zhang]] for his studio album ''[[Namanana]]''.<ref>{{cite web|title=EXO Lay prerelease slated for Oct. 5|url=http://kpopherald.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=201809281446229468313_2|website=KPOPHERALD|access-date=10 October 2018|archive-date=29 September 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180929155934/http://kpopherald.koreaherald.com/view.php?ud=201809281446229468313_2|url-status=live}}</ref>

In April 2019, Bazzi released "Caught in the Fire" and "[[Paradise (Bazzi song)|Paradise]]".<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.mtv.com/news/3119487/bazzi-paradise-video/|title=Bazzi Takes You To 'Paradise' In His Blissful New Video|last=Roth|first=Madeline|website=MTV News|language=en|access-date=2019-04-04|archive-date=2019-04-05|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190405125445/http://www.mtv.com/news/3119487/bazzi-paradise-video/|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://justnje.com/listen-to-bazzis-new-single-caught-in-the-fire/|title=Listen to Bazzi's new single, Caught In The Fire|date=April 3, 2019 |access-date=2019-04-04|archive-date=2019-04-04|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190404224727/https://justnje.com/listen-to-bazzis-new-single-caught-in-the-fire/|url-status=live}}</ref> On August 8, 2019, he released his debut mixtape ''[[Soul Searching (mixtape)|Soul Searching]]'', which includes the song "Paradise", as well as "[[Focus (Bazzi song)|Focus]]" (featuring [[21 Savage]]) and "[[I.F.L.Y.]]".

In 2020 Bazzi released the singles "Young & Alive",<ref>{{Cite web|date=2020-03-11|title=Bazzi Returns With Nostalgic New Single "Young & Alive"|url=https://www.spin.com/2020/03/bazzi-young-alive/|access-date=2021-01-25|website=Spin}}</ref> "Renee's Song", "I Got You", "I Don't Think I'm Okay",<ref>{{Cite web|date=2020-07-09|title=Bazzi opens up about low point in his life with new song, "I Don't Think I'm Okay"|url=https://www.wrmf.com/bazzi-opens-up-about-low-point-in-his-life-with-new-song-i-dont-think-im-okay/|access-date=2021-01-25|website=97.9 WRMF|language=en-US}}</ref> and "Crazy".<ref>{{Cite web|last=Hype|first=The Musical|date=2020-08-25|title=Bazzi, Crazy {{!}} Track Review 🎵|url=https://www.themusicalhype.com/bazzi-crazy-track-review/|access-date=2021-01-25|website=The Musical Hype|language=en-US}}</ref>

In a ''Billboard'' interview in 2018, Bazzi mentioned that he did not have any other job experiences before his music career.

On September 16, 2022, Bazzi released the long-awaited album ''Infinite Dreams''. Marking his first album in 4 years since ''Cosmic''. The album includes a total of 19 tracks. Bazzi announced his upcoming Infinite Dream Tour following the release of his album. The tour stopped in sixteen cities.

== Personal life ==
Bazzi lives in [[Los Angeles]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bazzi releases tribute - Music News - ABC News Radio|url=http://abcnewsradioonline.com/music-news/2020/4/1/bazzi-releases-tribute-to-girlfriend-of-two-years-renees-son.html|access-date=2021-01-25|website=abcnewsradioonline.com|language=en|archive-date=July 6, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210706092216/https://platform.tumblr.com/v1/share.js|url-status=dead}}</ref> He has talked openly about his struggles with mental health and substance abuse while quarantining during the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Freedman|first=Adrianna|date=2020-05-18|title=This Is How Bazzi Is Taking Care of His Mental Health in Quarantine|url=https://www.menshealth.com/entertainment/a32581394/bazzi-music-mental-health-chat/|access-date=2021-01-25|website=Men's Health|language=en-US}}</ref> In an open letter on Twitter, he stated that he "let a drug problem get out of hand, I've been drinking my boredom away."<ref>{{Cite web|title=Bazzi Admits to Letting 'Drug Problem Get Out of Hand' amid Pandemic: 'I've Been Very Unhappy'|url=https://people.com/music/bazzi-admits-to-drug-problems-during-quarantine/|access-date=2021-01-25|website=PEOPLE.com|language=EN}}</ref> He dated Renee Herbert.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://gizmostory.com/are-bazzi-and-renee-herbert-still-together-in-2022/ | title=Are Bazzi and Renee Herbert Still Together in 2022? | date=June 21, 2022 }}</ref>

